I reluctantly agree.  But I do think that setting up a trap should cost
the use of the wand in question, with some obvious exceptions such as the
current wand of digging capability.

I suggest setting up traps as follows: You begin by Engraving an appropriate
"powerful rune", and then lay an object on the engraving.  Wands of fire,
sleep, and cold produce the appropriate permanent trap.  Scrolls of fire and
potions of paralysis produce one-shot traps.  A pile of arrows or darts
would make an n-shot arrow/dart trap - but #dip them in a potion of poison
first for real effect!  Scrolls of teleport would produce one-shot teleport
traps - and so would scrolls of gold-detection if there was a bank on the
same level (guess where you go?).  Perhaps if the scroll were blessed first,
then the trap would be permanent.  Naturally, all attempts at producing a
trap with a cursed item would meet with various unfortunate results.

A possible advantage of this approach would be the Engraved word.  In
particular, I believe that these should be "learned" by the character in
the course of the game.  Such learning could come from pleasing the gods,
the oracle, maybe even from fortune cookies.

